    "md5": "3651c6e5d43ce206af6e18c83f5ac98d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1878,
    "chunk_text": "Following the circulation of media footage relating to the incident, the Ilavalai Police instituted legal proceedings against me despite the fact that I never used the firearm and merely possessed it for personal protection. The matter is presently before courts and the firearm remains in the custody of the Magistrate\u2019s Court of Mallakam.\n\nI reiterate that I have never wished to engage in politics while carrying a firearm. The unfortunate\n\n313 314\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4\n\nFurthermore, I wish to place before Parliament that prior to the above incident, I had already filed proceedings before the Magistrate\u2019s Court of Mallakam concerning death threats directed against me by certain Members of the Ilankai Tamil Arasu Kachchi and certain Pradeshiya Sabha members. At those proceedings, three separate voice recordings were produced and the preliminary investigation indicated that the voices matched those of the individuals responsible for making the threats. Those incidents demonstrate that the threats to my life and safety are real, serious and directly connected to my political activities.\n\nIn light of these circumstances, I respectfully submit that the continued failure to provide adequate security to me as a Member of Parliament constitutes a serious breach of Parliamentary Privileges and interferes with my ability to discharge my constitutional duties freely and without fear.\n\nAccordingly, I seek leave to raise a Question of Privilege against -\n\n1. the Hon. Anura Kumara Dissanayake, Minister of Defence; 2. the Hon. Deputy Minister of Defence; and 3. Mr. Priyantha Weerasooriya, Inspector General of Police\n\nfor their failure to ensure the provision of adequate security and protection to me as a duly elected Member of Parliament despite repeated warnings, representations, complaints and documented threats to my life and safety."
