    "chunk_index": 66,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7054ea62d4ab5a0e8b1d247b7bcdaafc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1931,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, efficient dispute resolution also has a positive impact on the economy. Litigation delays have an adverse impact on trade, business and commerce, which, in turn, impacts on economic progress. That is a negative feature which is often not acknowledged. The need for smarter dispute resolution for the business sector devoid of expense, delay and unpredictability is important for economic development and to attract investors. The business and commercial community must have access to smart conflict resolution options that are time-efficient and cost-effective. Productivity is obviously enhanced due to these benefits with a significant impact on the economy. Businesses, whether large corporates or small enterprises, should be able to focus on their core objectives without being detracted by long-drawn legal battles.\n\n487 488\n\n\u0dd1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0d9c\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nto be accepted as an investor-friendly destination, the options for dispute resolution must be diverse and must offer internationally accepted methods that are not bogged down by the notorious evils of delay and expense as meaningful dispute resolution offers significant economic advantages.\n\nSir, mediation is a more meaningful process for certain categories of disputes with better prospects for sustainable settlement. It is accepted that certain categories of disputes are more meaningfully resolved using a process that is non-adversarial and which accords primacy to address the needs and interests of disputants in a creative way. Mediation is known to provide prospects to reduce instances where a dispute leads to the termination of a commercial relationship. This benefit is also articulated in the Preamble to the 2018 UN Mediation Convention. Settlements that are based on terms agreed to by disputants assure the sustainability of the outcome, as opposed to an outcome handed down by a third party such as through the adjudicatory process."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
