    "chunk_index": 67,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "ec7abc40a4e55eae956fc9444244ce7f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1835,
    "chunk_text": "Sir, mediation is a more meaningful process for certain categories of disputes with better prospects for sustainable settlement. It is accepted that certain categories of disputes are more meaningfully resolved using a process that is non-adversarial and which accords primacy to address the needs and interests of disputants in a creative way. Mediation is known to provide prospects to reduce instances where a dispute leads to the termination of a commercial relationship. This benefit is also articulated in the Preamble to the 2018 UN Mediation Convention. Settlements that are based on terms agreed to by disputants assure the sustainability of the outcome, as opposed to an outcome handed down by a third party such as through the adjudicatory process.\n\nThe role and the duties of mediators, disputants and service providers are set out in the Bill, Sir. The details of the mediation process are also set out. That is, the steps to be taken to initiate a mediation and to bring the sessions to a closure, the salient features that are intrinsic to the conduct of mediation sessions and the observance of confidentiality with regard to matters discussed in a mediation. The without prejudice rule is also recognized.\n\nSir, reference of disputes to mediation by courts is provided for in the Bill and it is a very common feature in many jurisdictions around the world. The concept of a mediation clause including the pre-dispute mediation clause is recognized by it. That is the same as the arbitration clause in arbitrations. Disputants can voluntarily agree to mediate even without a pre-dispute mediation clause. Where there is a mediation clause or where a mediation has commenced voluntarily, no action can be filed in court unless mediation has failed. Prescription ceases to run when mediation is resorted to until closure."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-06-11-2026-06-11",
    "num": "2026-06-11",
