    "chunk_text": "Govi Sathiya 2012 10\n\n2013 13\n\n2014 43.12\n\n\u201cWasa Wisa Nethi Hetak\u201d Production of Organic Fertilizer\n\n2018 6.9\n\n\u201cSaru Piri Gewaththak\u201d 2018 22.23\n\n\u201cApi Wawalai Api Kanne\u201d (Planting one million jackfruit plants)\n\n2018 8.0\n\n\u201cSaubhagya\u201d Nation-al Home Gardening Programme\n\n2022 107.31\n\nYouth Retention in Agriculture Pro-gramme (Youth Village Programme)\n\n2023 108.51\n\nYouth Agri-Entrepreneurship Village Programme\n\n2024 333.84\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2 23\n\nAccordingly, a growth of 7 per cent was achieved in the agriculture sector in the year 2010 and notably, the growth in paddy production sector recorded a high value of 17.5 per cent compared to previous year. However, the heavy rainfall and flooding that occurred in the last month of 2010 and the first month of 2011 negatively impacted the growth of the agriculture sector.\n\nWhen considering the national contribution of the agriculture sector in 2011, a very low growth of 1.5 per cent was recorded in comparison to the 7 per cent growth in 2010. This was due to the adverse weather conditions, specifically the floods that prevailed at the beginning of the year in the Anuradhapura, Polonnaruwa, Trincomalee, Ampara and Batticaloa Districts. It also caused a certain setback in the growth of the paddy production sector.\n\nIn the year 2012, numerous sub-programmes were implemented to contribute positively toward the aforementioned criteria. These included improving soil conservation and water management in cultivation lands, model villages programme for food security and post-harvest management, programmes to increase fruit production, community-based seed production village project and programmes related to post-harvest technology.\n\nBy the year 2013, as a result of the development programmes implemented under the contribution and guidance of the Ministry of Agriculture, the country achieved self-sufficiency in rice and was able to produce the major portion of the domestic maize requirement. Furthermore,"
