    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0ddb\u0dc0\u0daf\u200d) \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db8\u0db1\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dca \u0d85\u0dcf\u0da0\u0dca\u0da0\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb5\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bb0\u0bcd) \u0b87\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0bae\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bc1\u0ba9\u0bbe) (The Hon. (Dr.) Ramanathan Archchuna) Four hundred and thirty. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc2\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dca \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0da2\u0db4\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dc3\u0dca \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0dca\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0baf\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9c\u0baa\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0b87\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. Shanakiyan Rajaputhiran Rasamanickam) It is 430, according to the Hon. (Dr.) Ramanathan Archchuna. The scale of these findings raises serious questions regarding identification of victims, forensic investigations, accountability and the measures taken by the Government to establish the truth.\n\nIn this regard, will the Hon. Minister inform this House -\n\n(a) what the total number of skeletal remains recovered from the Chemmani excavation site is, as of the latest official count;\n\n(c) how many of the recovered remains have undergone forensic examination, DNA analysis or other scientific identification procedures and how many have been positively identified;\n\n(d) what measures have been taken to establish the identity of the victims, the cause and the approximate period of death; and\n\n(e) whether the Government has sought or received technical assistance, forensic expertise or DNA analysis support from international institutions or foreign governments in relation to the Chemmani excavations; if so, what the details are thereof?\n\nHon. Minister, since there is a 350-word count to adhere to with regard to this particular Question, I could not go into detail. I raise this Question because, as you are also aware, in 1996, during the Krishanthi Kumaraswamy excavation, around 15 skeletal remains were sent to Scotland, out of which two were identified. The balance 13 skeletal remains not unidentified remain at the University of Lancashire. So, their custodian is the University of Lancashire, I believe. If you are really serious about identifying them really fast, all that the Government needs to do is to write a letter and ask, \"Could you give us expertise?\" I have just concluded a\n\n1249 1250\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2 25"
