    "chunk_size_bytes": 2286,
    "chunk_text": "Obviously, one of the reasons for my visit was to make sure that things are functioning smoothly and that funds are available because we cannot drag this on forever. But, only when I saw how the investigations are being carried out painstakingly with little brushes and everything that I realized how complicated this job could be. As much as myself, my Government, even you as a Representative and the people are in a rush and a hurry to find things out and I also do understand that time is taken, but I can assure you that the truth will be found, it will be dealt with and that our Government has no business in covering anything up. - [Interruption.]\n\n1253 1254\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0dba\u0da5 \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd \u0db1\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf \u0dca\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2 25\n\nFinally, I welcome the fact that you all have sealed the \"Gun Site\" of the camp and investigations on senior military officials like the former Navy Commander have started again. So, we welcome all that, but like I cautioned the Hon. Prime Minister a year ago also, 40 per cent of the Government\u2019s first term is coming to an end in September. Therefore, before the honeymoon period ends, you have to get these difficult, controversial and contagious things dealt with.\n\nThank you. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u200d \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Minister, would you like to respond to that? Be brief, please.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0db1\u0da5 \u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0dc2\u0dab\u0dba \u0db1\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dc3 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bb7\u0ba9 \u0ba8\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bb0) (The Hon. Harshana Nanayakkara, Attorney-at-Law) Hon. Rasamanickam, thank you so much. I think you are saying the right thing and I am also saying the same thing, but from a different level. Are we going to get international expertise? Of course, we are. But, this is a compact situation, where the court will inform us that\n\nthese, these things need to be done. So, it is only at that point we can figure out which international agency or international body has the capacity and the reputation to delivery it. So that, we will do, but only when it comes to that."
