    "chunk_text": "1. The reason for the deviation of headline inflation from the lower side of the target since Quarter 2, 2024 have been explained in detail in the Reports submitted to Parliament under Section 26(5) of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka Act, No. 16 of 2023, Those reports are publicly available on the Bank\u2019s website as well. It is important to note that inflation measures the rate of change in general prices rather than the level of prices. Following the sharp increase in the overall price level during the high inflation episode in 2022, prices remain elevated compared to the pre-crisis levels. As a result, households may continue to experience a high cost of living even in an environment of relatively low inflation. The Central Bank\u2019s Monetary Policy Report - February 2026 provides further information."
