    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "a101f81ed23d4d0f9bd33dbed384aaa7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1608,
    "chunk_text": "There are seven members in the Governing Board namely, Dr. P. Nandalal Weerasinghe, Chairman; Mr. Nihal Fonseka, Appointed Member; Dr. Ravi Rathnayake, Appointed Member; Mr. Anushka Wijesinha, Appointed Member; Mr. Vish Govindasamy, Appointed Member; Mr. Manil Jayesinghe, Appointed Member and Mr. Maithri Evan Wickremesinghe, P.C., Appointed Member.\n\n6. Under the Central Bank Act, the primary objective of the Central Bank is achieving and maintaining domestic price stability, while the other objective is to secure financial system stability. That Act also states that, without prejudice to these objectives, the Central Bank shall support the general economic policy framework of the Government, as provided by law. In pursuing price stability, the Central Bank is also required to take into account the stabilization of output towards its potential level. Accordingly, while the Act does not specify separate statutory targets for variables such as growth, employment or external sector indicators, these broader macroeconomic conditions are taken into account in the conduct of monetary policy within the framework established under the Act.\n\nAccordingly, in monetary policy deliberations and arriving at monetary policy decisions, the Central Bank would take into account the broader economic conditions such as economic growth, employment, developments in the external sector and financial system stability. While the Central Bank may consider such broader economic conditions when formulating policy, the Central Bank Act does not explicitly set statutory targets for these macroeconomic variables."
