    "chunk_text": "pretend to be part of the drug cartels, infiltrate those organizations and go to the source. Unfortunately, Hon. Minister, we do not have such a mechanism. So, I would ask you to look at other jurisdictions where the law enforcement officers pretend to be drug lords, infiltrate the drug mafia and then go to the source. Until we have such a legal framework, we would not be able to go the source. Therefore, the Minister could look into it and we could appoint a Select Committee specifically to look at establishing such a legal mechanism through which we could penetrate the drug cartels. All over the world, they have succeeded by penetrating the drug cartels.\n\nSir, today, various drugs are used by people of various walks of life. Heroin and ICE are used by a certain strata of the society and cocaine is used by the higher strata of the society. So, every class of the society has a different drug to facilitate their want, but the end result is, the youth in this country are getting destroyed, unless we take serious measures.\n\nSir, I think this topic is not political. I think we need every Hon. Member of Parliament to be active in his electorate, going to schools, temples, churches and mosques and speaking to the priests, the Catholic priests, the Moulvis and seeing how we could work together as a community to eradicate this problem. What is the story the drug cartel tells our youth? They say, \"You can live in a fancy world; you would not have worries\". That is why our youth are being attracted to drugs. Therefore, I would ask the Hon. Minister to, as much as steps are taken to"
